      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix #99163: harden large chat attachment parsing",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nLarge clipboard image data URLs currently pass through whole-string base64 validation and full-payload MIME sniffing. For multi-megabyte attachments this does unnecessary work on the hot path and can make attachment parsing much more expensive than the small header sniff actually needs.\n\n## Summary\n\n- replace chat attachment base64 validation regex with an iterative scanner so large clipboard payloads avoid whole-string regexp matching\n- move the stack-safe large-payload fix into `canonicalizeBase64`, preserving full malformed-tail validation for shared callers\n- make MIME sniffing decode only a small canonical base64 prefix after full payload validation\n- add regression coverage for ~1.9MB PNG clipboard data URLs, large shared canonicalization, and malformed data after a valid PNG prefix\n\nFixes #99163.\n\n## Evidence\n\nReal Gateway parser proof using a generated valid PNG data URL on this PR head:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"proof\": \"gateway chat.send attachment parser large PNG data URL\",\n  \"pngBytes\": 1901669,\n  \"base64Chars\": 2535560,\n  \"dataUrlChars\": 2535582,\n  \"elapsedMs\": 375,\n  \"images\": 1,\n  \"imageMime\": \"image/png\",\n  \"imageDataMatchesInput\": true,\n  \"offloadedRefs\": 0,\n  \"imageOrder\": [\n    \"inline\"\n  ],\n  \"message\": \"proof: large Control UI clipboard image\",\n  \"result\": \"ok-no-RangeError\"\n}\n```\n\nProof command:\n\n- `node_modules/.bin/tsx /tmp/openclaw-99213-gateway-proof.ts` generated a 745x745 valid PNG, wrapped it as `data:image/png;base64,...`, and passed it through `parseMessageWithAttachments()` from `src/gateway/chat-attachments.ts`.\n\nValidation:\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs packages/media-core/src/base64.test.ts src/media/sniff-mime-from-base64.test.ts src/gateway/chat-attachments.test.ts --reporter=verbose` — 127 passed across media-core, media sniffing, and gateway shards\n- `OPENCLAW_OXLINT_SKIP_PREPARE=1 node scripts/run-oxlint.mjs packages/media-core/src/base64.ts packages/media-core/src/base64.test.ts src/media/sniff-mime-from-base64.ts src/media/sniff-mime-from-base64.test.ts src/gateway/chat-attachments.ts src/gateway/chat-attachments.test.ts` — passed\n- `node scripts/run-tsgo.mjs -p test/tsconfig/tsconfig.core.test.non-agents.json --incremental --tsBuildInfoFile .artifacts/tsgo-cache/core-test-non-agents.tsbuildinfo` — passed\n- `node_modules/.bin/oxfmt --check --threads=1 packages/media-core/src/base64.ts packages/media-core/src/base64.test.ts src/media/sniff-mime-from-base64.ts src/media/sniff-mime-from-base64.test.ts src/gateway/chat-attachments.ts src/gateway/chat-attachments.test.ts` — passed\n- `git diff --check` — passed\n\nNote: this revision preserves the shared `sniffMimeFromBase64` full-input validation contract that ClawSweeper flagged. A valid PNG prefix with an invalid base64 tail now returns `undefined`, while large valid payloads still sniff from a bounded decoded prefix and avoid full-payload `Buffer.from(..., \"base64\")` on the gateway path.\n",
        "branch": "fix/chat-attachment-stack-99163",
        "head_sha": "c637cac42f0002eaa921fb51bc99c7ba9222fe81",
